/// What this build's Leitmotif listens to, for the "What is this?" page.
enum Edition {
    static let name = "Ambit"
    static let leitmotifSource = "Your iPhone's own life, read on the phone: its motion (footsteps, resting or in your hand, how it's held), the charger and battery, headphones and other audio, Wi-Fi or cellular, Low Power Mode, heat, the screen's brightness, and its network counters (how many bytes it sends and receives, never what is in them). No location, no names, no content, no VPN; nothing is recorded or sent anywhere."
    static let leitmotifMapping = "Each kind of event has its own leitmotif of two to four notes, so the charger, headphones, Wi-Fi or a walk always sound like themselves, and the opposite event (unplugging, taking them off, stopping) is the same tune backwards. Footsteps become soft high notes while you walk or run. Traffic is cut into bursts, each a letter by direction and size; every three-letter word seeds its own motif, so a habit (streaming, messaging, scrolling) gets the same tune each time. Movement and the screen set how bright the piano is, a low battery tires it, and resting flat on a table hushes it. Download rate sets how hard the keys are struck, upload rate how much tape dust rides along."
}
